  "equipment_type": "Sensor (ultrasonic wind)",
  "applies_to": "WM80 sensors with RS-485 in Modbus mode (e.g. ordering option C), per user guide M212995EN-F.",
  "summary": "The Vaisala WM80 is a heated ultrasonic wind sensor aimed at uses that need continuous wind data, such as wind turbine control, ship navigation and dynamic positioning. On RS-485 it serves Modbus RTU or an ASCII/NMEA message. This map covers wind speed and direction (sample, instant, average, gust, lull, U/V components), sonic temperature, averaging and heating settings, serial settings, status words, monitoring values and test registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "The guide prints each register as a hex address with its decimal value (used on the wire) plus a 'register number' equal to the address + 1. Wind speed sample is at address 0x0000 (register number 1)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "WM80 User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M212995EN-F",
    "revision_date": "2025-12",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M212995EN-F/en-US",
    "pages": "pp. 38-39 (Modbus RTU protocol, data types), 72-80 (Appendix B registers)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16; function 43 (0x2B) reads device ID.",
    "int32 and float values are two registers in little-endian word order (least significant word first, CDAB), as the guide's data-type table states. Bytes inside each register are big-endian.",
    "Ordering option C ships as Modbus RTU, 19200 bps, N, 8, 2, address 240; the register table also lists 19200 and N82 as defaults.",
    "Left out: the analog output 1/2 settings (Tables 57-58), the diagnostic code int32 registers (reserved for Vaisala diagnostics), product order code, manufacturing date and product name."
  ],
